# Epic: Innate Pharmacy Coverage and Explicit Immune Role Boundaries

**Epic ID:** `EPIC-OE-EIS-001`
**AuthorityEffect:** None
**Status:** `LIVE`

**Lifecycle scope:** LIVE — current coverage verification
**Date:** October 2026
**Target Crates:** `core_prompt_civilization`, `core_epistemic_immune_system`
**Prior Art Grounding:** `LIB-016808`, `LIB-016952` (source references, not runtime evidence)

## Current implementation and bounded behavior

[NativePharmacy](../../../../eis/infrastructure/native_pharmacy.py) invokes [core_prompt_civilization::pharmacy](../../../../engine/crates_rs/core_prompt_civilization/src/pharmacy.rs) for eleven shared structural failure classes. PERSONA_AUTHORITY_LEAK is currently a [Python host check](../../../../eis/domain/host_checks.py). The combined [PharmacyMatcher](../../../../eis/infrastructure/mssn_ports.py) must retain this provenance distinction.

The [existing parity suite](../../../../eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_parity.py) documents Python/native differences including persona handling, truthiness and text/hash representations. Verify each declared shared class separately; do not advertise twelve native classes or universal parity.

The seven role names remain an architectural separation: detector specification, fixtures, evaluation evidence, external decision, telemetry, regulation and tolerance screening. Names alone do not prove separate custody or external authority.

## Residual work and acceptance

Verify concrete positive/negative loci through the native port; fail closed on unavailable/malformed native responses. Retain candidate/source binding in combined reports. A clean report means no enumerated rule fired in that finite input; it neither authenticates a human decision nor promotes a candidate.

Admission, activation, thymus and telemetry are separate ports owned by EIS-002/EIS-003. No fallback may convert unavailable native execution into a clean report. No broad claim about hallucination elimination or mathematical verification follows from structural matching.

## Obstruction review and TDD test plan

**Review basis (2026-10-10):** NativePharmacy currently delegates eleven shared classes to core_prompt_civilization::pharmacy. PERSONA_AUTHORITY_LEAK is a separate Python host check, and the existing parity tests document additional bounded differences. A native skip cannot establish parity or native availability.

**Bounded behavior and public port:** Call NativePharmacy.detect(candidate_json,DetectionContext) and the combined PharmacyMatcher.match_antigen port with a real built native host. Compare native shared-class loci against literal expected paths; run the separate persona host check explicitly. A clean report has AuthorityEffect None and is not admission.

**Dependencies and review routing:** Implement one case at a time after the stated dependency is available. Syntax Prefilter checks malformed input; Bare Metal Anchor/Techne implements the smallest production change; Defect Hunter and the Inspector challenge the independent oracle; Punchlist checks custody before Adversary records the scoped result. Use the four stages intake, implementation, adversarial QA, and receipt review. Stop after at most three repair attempts and retain the blocking witness.

| Order | RED witness → minimal GREEN → refactor | Proposed test and independent oracle |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | A shared-class positive candidate and nearly identical clean negative must differ at the expected locus; correct only that native rule; refactor after exact loci are stable. | Extend `eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_parity.py::test_shared_class_positive_and_negative_loci`; hand-authored JSON/path fixtures for one class, then add classes individually. |
| 2 | PERSONA_AUTHORITY_LEAK must be reported by the explicit host check without pretending native coverage; implement only combined-report attribution; reject duplicate or mislabeled provenance. | Proposed `eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_role_partition.py::test_persona_host_check_has_separate_provenance`; exact class code, source and loci oracle. |
| 3 | Missing native binary, malformed native response or transplanted candidate digest must fail closed; preserve typed unavailable/binding errors; restore host and recover the same native result. | Extend `eis/tests/unit/test_native_pharmacy_adapter.py::test_native_unavailable_and_binding_refuse`; real positive native test plus isolated boundary faults. |
| 4 | A clean native report injected into an admission request must not admit a candidate; add a port-level fence if missing; an external valid admission path remains a separate positive control. | Proposed `eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_role_partition.py::test_clean_report_does_not_admit`; status remains CANDIDATE and no admission receipt appears. |

**Decisive mutation and theoretical minimum:** INVARIANT: the bounded behavior above. BREAK: the negative inputs in the ordered slices. WITNESS: actual returned value/refusal plus persisted bytes or send counts, compared with the stated independent oracle. MUTATION: Disable one shared class in [pharmacy.rs](../../../../engine/crates_rs/core_prompt_civilization/src/pharmacy.rs) and require its positive locus test to fail; change the unavailable-host refusal in [native_pharmacy.py](../../../../eis/infrastructure/native_pharmacy.py) to empty findings and require the negative availability witness to fail. Source existence was checked for this plan; mutation execution and RED recovery are still prospective. Do not count a mock-only verdict or a skipped native test as verification.

**Proposed small-batch commands:** Run each named test first with `-k <test_name>` to demonstrate RED, implement the minimum GREEN, then run the one-file regression command below before refactoring. Paths labeled proposed are not claimed to exist. Commands are not execution receipts.

~~~powershell
cargo test --manifest-path engine/crates_rs/Cargo.toml -p core_prompt_civilization -j 1 pharmacy
py -3.12 -m pytest eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_parity.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest eis/tests/unit/test_native_pharmacy_adapter.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest eis/tests/unit/test_pharmacy_role_partition.py -q
~~~

**Cross-epic sink ownership:** EIS owns detector/support/activation/regulation evidence; the external admission/trust decision remains outside learned candidates. Adversary can challenge and route findings but cannot admit them. Providers and PFP consume typed findings through explicit adapters, preserving EIS provenance and subject/rule digests. A producer supplies immutable source evidence; the consumer validates its own contract and emits its own scoped receipt. No downstream plan may reuse a producer PASS as an admission decision.

**Scope and evidence ceiling:** Parity is limited to shared classes and documented representation semantics. Native host absence is a blocker, not a successful fallback. No finite detector panel establishes semantic completeness. Record any eventual SoftwareQaReceiptV1 with exact command, runtime version, exit status, tested scope, base/head and source digests, failing input, mutation diff, and recovery output outside `plans/epics/`. This planning update executes none of these proposed tests and grants no runtime or admission authority.


Cross-epic ownership and retained custody follow the [integration decision](../../decisions/adr_20261010_epic_integration_ownership.md).
